{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/ST"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IntervalTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The intervals are kept in an AVL tree ordered by lower bound, then upper bound, then the order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were inserted in, and each vertex also records the largest upper bound in its subtree, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a search skips every subtree that ends before the query begins (Cormen, Leiserson, Rivest and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Stein, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Introduction to Algorithms"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", §14.3). The same interval may be stored more than once,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with different values.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code"